{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-49811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(1,2),(1,0),$ and $(-1,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,2)}=2(1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,0)}=2(1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-2)}=2(-1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(-2)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/3dcb95f44f53f046c543d281038c0ac03fb14357cecdb7b96d5f41d33e9b0ed6.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-49811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087964b8ca102ac79eef50e9c2ad0114a044ecc1e3f0d01eccf8b3c4ea641a31"} {"question" "q-49811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-