8/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-80497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x-2y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-80497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,-1),(2,-1),$ and $(2,1).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-1)}=(-2)-2(-1)=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-1)}=(2)-2(-1)=4, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,1)}=(2)-2(1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/6a2d6f3812df2844171dacf1675d8e3d90167010cb2ffcf939f88d9cfcafe8a9.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-80497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087964b8ca102ac79eef50e9c2ad0114a044ecc1e3f0d01eccf8b3c4ea641a31"} {"question" "q-80497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-80497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/1b8e42e667d2fe4c713e92f879c9894e826fdbe3e6928addb3c4b36ce71991e0.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/2527ad3b4f6d0a1d84a9e907b5e3e9bddee439fbd17c2a1a4c3ca8c418f65293.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/327d6ae536cd6d76eff01387b51a4d2cc0522559d6ec6d02e3a86c2a3977f7b2.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/3ddcc5784dc1fd60ba3c95ecda373678d00fc6c45e6b5e5655febcc130c37d95.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/e7e267508d68c1d4eeb31509a4a2957e120cecab920481ba6dc2b0fa1f84433b.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-80497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/3ddcc5784dc1fd60ba3c95ecda373678d00fc6c45e6b5e5655febcc130c37d95.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-1,-2),(2,-2)$ and $(2,2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-2)}=-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{(-1)}=4, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}=-2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,2)}=-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/5e6b2df4680cea04cda42312659c76ba713a025150ebcc547dddc2a6501aebf3.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087964b8ca102ac79eef50e9c2ad0114a044ecc1e3f0d01eccf8b3c4ea641a31"} {"question" "q-119674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/4afe9527d6ff39ce7f5325a4a35ce5095d9bf0b1beb2fcde4de86a977bdac9e8.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/5e6b2df4680cea04cda42312659c76ba713a025150ebcc547dddc2a6501aebf3.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/a0f75b52c741eca3322f4fe61009ba3c65e573f588edf9d3785019a1227f9769.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/c78c6d760cffb3dfb95233f9fc21dfea5a951371b056827885d1aa35469a458c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/d48911eaffd88e249ef115a5511bff979ffa0f848ef8a1e8556db07ad273e41a.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/5e6b2df4680cea04cda42312659c76ba713a025150ebcc547dddc2a6501aebf3.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-96089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x+2y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-96089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,1),(1,1),$ and $(2,1).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,1)}=-2+2(1)=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,1)}=1+2(1)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,1)}=2+2(1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/cc55a08f71cd75f0dda356149a61e9ab78536ecbb4644b88f840122863b92b88.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-96089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087964b8ca102ac79eef50e9c2ad0114a044ecc1e3f0d01eccf8b3c4ea641a31"} {"question" "q-96089" "field" "selection" "attri