 "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/7d5df9fe81ebd1e656eefc97380ae646a1a4f64de51e4745bc31d822e022d65d.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following could be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y-{x}^{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, the only one that varies with both $x$ and $y$ is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/1bd04b981c412d771617ffaaa7cedf88b063ae49ab567cd27d665eb381a1b648.png)\n\n  \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a vertical line and a horizontal line, the slopes vary if we move along either of the two lines.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/83f2ac528d0e4bdd7e486284a9f3d5692e0111c5cdc58dcc554e12dd0185f15f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087964b8ca102ac79eef50e9c2ad0114a044ecc1e3f0d01eccf8b3c4ea641a31"} {"question" "q-119369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/1bd04b981c412d771617ffaaa7cedf88b063ae49ab567cd27d665eb381a1b648.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/7470460ab6f2d7e0bfde9585c6447a75abbea498d9c0628c23d6b69bc9738c46.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/b9498bdcc8a1bfb59c3db6053873a9622a2d936cc9a885f1b2bf8a40b1ec0b93.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/d8a84684bd0ea9b96e9e3901b4dfec5e5568a80ad44202161a76414ce0a4edfa.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/f5ee96c6ad4540cde69b78af9a13e4513a24f6c537f69c4bee5ec0d440da56c2.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/1bd04b981c412d771617ffaaa7cedf88b063ae49ab567cd27d665eb381a1b648.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)$ varies with both $x$ and $y,$ which of the following **cannot** be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $x$ given a fixed value of $y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/9cb42cde56fcbea0c489742cab1448890728dab584395129b21794115b1e1298.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/9d256bd6c44a9abc8489c360722b5c5e8243f0d4a9aa6fee03cad52e5334b385.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119383" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087964b8ca102ac79eef50e9c2ad0114a044ecc1e3f0d01eccf8b3c4ea641a31"} {"question" "q-119383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/state.json" "file_sha256" "e9998b3a797dafe075b85e111d40d0eff1ffd5a8b5ff1b1b8fbb63555f37a017"} {"question" "q-119383" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/96817ea42e1d860db97d3ee6bca79e9a8b03a0fd413c87ebc5679f746da3166b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/9cb42cde56fcbea0c489742cab1448890728dab584395129b21794115b1e1298.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/ac12c64fe5282c78ea926eec823cec6b66c8fad9f153c4191d39ba7751e90e25.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/c959785ef067b41eba5e5ca5f0759acdd81c9f613c92854ba5937be6bced2c86.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/fe57c0cc2d75729921eb46408e0e4a6932eba06c0